00:24:53.610 --> 00:24:56.620
Show, in case they had any cameras.

00:24:56.620 --> 00:25:00.320
Then we walked into the, it
was like a reception area.

00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:05.276
And we stood side by side, and
Dickie knocked on the door,

00:25:05.276 --> 00:25:07.183
and the people, guy looked out,

00:25:08.300 --> 00:25:10.690
he showed a card, investigated.

00:25:10.690 --> 00:25:12.143
We understand there's gonna,

00:25:13.136 --> 00:25:14.877
do you have a problem over there?

00:25:14.877 --> 00:25:16.040
And the guy opened up the door.

00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:17.843
So he opened up the door, we run in.

00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:20.400
There was two brothers, jewelers.

00:25:20.400 --> 00:25:22.173
They were Jewish guys.

00:25:22.173 --> 00:25:24.093
Zimmerman, I think their
name was, I'm not sure.

00:25:24.930 --> 00:25:27.220
And the New York jeweler, so we got 'em,

00:25:27.220 --> 00:25:28.123
we taped 'em up,

00:25:29.076 --> 00:25:30.900
and I noticed the windows were up, blinds.

00:25:30.900 --> 00:25:33.330
So I closed the blinds,
and I go to the safe

00:25:34.220 --> 00:25:37.380
while he's going through their pockets.

00:25:37.380 --> 00:25:41.377
There's a bag, a pouch
this big, he got it.

00:25:41.377 --> 00:25:42.979
He said, "I got it."

00:25:42.979 --> 00:25:43.930
So I says, "Come here."

00:25:43.930 --> 00:25:47.136
He comes over, I say,
"Fucking safe's open."

00:25:47.136 --> 00:25:48.958
There's nothing in the safe.

00:25:48.958 --> 00:25:50.770
He went, shh, he went like that.

00:25:50.770 --> 00:25:53.277
He picked up on it before I did.

00:25:53.277 --> 00:25:54.327
It was an inside job.

00:25:55.170 --> 00:25:57.023
The jewelers cleaned out the safe.

00:25:58.150 --> 00:26:00.633
When he seen the safe,
the kid was sharp, Dickie.

00:26:01.799 --> 00:26:03.340
Rich, I call him Dickie all the time.

00:26:03.340 --> 00:26:06.495
I said, "Ah, these mother fuckers, ah."

00:26:06.495 --> 00:26:07.328
I went like that.

00:26:07.328 --> 00:26:12.328
So I got all this shit,
and I hand it to Dickie.

00:26:12.727 --> 00:26:14.819
And he says, I'm gonna go down,

00:26:14.819 --> 00:26:17.673
and I'm gonna wait by the "L" for you.

00:26:18.700 --> 00:26:22.460
I waited five, ten minutes
with these guys in the room.

00:26:22.460 --> 00:26:24.334
Now, when I was sure he was

00:26:24.334 --> 00:26:26.760
out of the building, then I went down.

00:26:26.760 --> 00:26:30.080
Same routine, elevator,
or I walked two flights

00:26:30.080 --> 00:26:33.530
down the elevator, walked a
flight, elevator, all right.

00:26:33.530 --> 00:26:35.684
'Cause them gates come down.

00:26:35.684 --> 00:26:38.000
These guys scream robbery,
boom, the gates come down.

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:39.341
You ain't going nowhere.

00:26:39.341 --> 00:26:40.340
- [Mark] Then you're stuck.

00:26:40.340 --> 00:26:42.145
- So I go down, I meet him at the subway.

00:26:42.145 --> 00:26:44.322
We jump on the "L," boom,
we go to Forest Park,

00:26:44.322 --> 00:26:47.180
We go to Mannheim Road,

00:26:47.180 --> 00:26:51.100
where Tony Spilotro was in a
motel room with this guy, Mike,

00:26:51.100 --> 00:26:54.480
waiting for us to come
back with the goods.

00:26:54.480 --> 00:26:55.780
Cause he was gonna pay us.

00:26:56.785 --> 00:26:58.680
So I hand him, we hand him the stuff,

00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:00.910
but on the way there, of course,

00:27:00.910 --> 00:27:03.103
we're checking out the pouch,

00:27:04.260 --> 00:27:06.973
and they're all in, loose
diamonds in the wax paper.

00:27:08.540 --> 00:27:11.161
Dickie says, "Man," he says,

00:27:11.161 --> 00:27:13.904
"We're getting less money than we should."

00:27:13.904 --> 00:27:14.780
He says, "Look at this."

00:27:14.780 --> 00:27:16.010
And I look, I said, "Holy, fuck."

00:27:16.010 --> 00:27:18.583
A lot of loose diamonds, I mean,

00:27:18.583 --> 00:27:20.753
you're talking a pouch
this full of diamonds.

00:27:22.438 --> 00:27:24.562
And I don't wanna name
how much money we get

00:27:24.562 --> 00:27:25.762
because I'm embarrassed,

00:27:26.620 --> 00:27:28.983
but I trusted my friend Tony, right?

00:27:29.990 --> 00:27:33.140
Wind up as Tony, and Mike and the Outfit

00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:35.070
made most of the money.

00:27:35.070 --> 00:27:36.790
So we got rid of it.

00:27:36.790 --> 00:27:37.806
We went back.

00:27:37.806 --> 00:27:38.639
Dickie went to his place.

00:27:38.639 --> 00:27:41.663
I went to the lounge, in
Elmwood Park there was a lounge.

00:27:42.987 --> 00:27:44.160
And we were watching the news guys,

00:27:44.160 --> 00:27:45.710
and then it comes over the air.

00:27:48.464 --> 00:27:50.650
It comes over the air,
right after the robbery now,

00:27:50.650 --> 00:27:51.870
it's only a matter of two hours.

00:27:51.870 --> 00:27:55.125
Big, they call it a $500,000 robbery,

00:27:55.125 --> 00:27:55.958
and it was the biggest robbery

00:27:55.958 --> 00:27:57.083
in Chicago history at the time.

00:27:58.388 --> 00:28:00.760
And I look and I go,
but I don't say nothing.

00:28:00.760 --> 00:28:03.170
Everybody's going, "Man,
them guys really got lucky."

00:28:03.170 --> 00:28:04.849
I wonder who they were.

00:28:04.849 --> 00:28:05.682
I'm sitting right with them.

00:28:05.682 --> 00:28:07.253
Fucking guys never knew it was me, right?

00:28:08.448 --> 00:28:12.293
Three days later, I get
pulled over by the detectives.

00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:16.209
They says "Hanhardt wants to talk to you."

00:28:16.209 --> 00:28:18.810
Hanhardt was in charge
of the robbery unit.

00:28:18.810 --> 00:28:20.946
I said, "What the fuck
does he want with me?"

00:28:20.946 --> 00:28:21.779
You know?

00:28:21.779 --> 00:28:23.081
So I go downtown, I go to,

00:28:23.081 --> 00:28:25.490
what is the name of it?

00:28:25.490 --> 00:28:27.304
It was a police station.

00:28:27.304 --> 00:28:28.440
I can't even think of the name of it now.

00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:32.690
Shakespeare, so I go there,
and I go up to his office.

00:28:32.690 --> 00:28:34.508
They take the cuffs off.

00:28:34.508 --> 00:28:35.790
He says, "You want some
coffee or a donut?"

00:28:35.790 --> 00:28:37.010
Seriously.

00:28:37.010 --> 00:28:39.197
And I goes, "No, what do you want?"

00:28:39.197 --> 00:28:40.590
"What's up?"

00:28:40.590 --> 00:28:43.540
He said, "I'd never fucking
believe it in a million years."

00:28:44.824 --> 00:28:45.657
"What, what are you
talking about?" I said.

00:28:45.657 --> 00:28:47.719
"What are you hauling me here for?"

00:28:47.719 --> 00:28:50.619
"It's you, fucking did that
robbery, the Maller Building."

00:28:51.751 --> 00:28:54.953
And I fucking said, "How
does this guy know that?"

00:28:55.808 --> 00:28:58.200
How did, I only been out of jail a week.

00:28:58.200 --> 00:29:00.592
I didn't even know he
knew I was out of jail,

00:29:00.592 --> 00:29:02.490
I said, "What are you talking about?"

00:29:02.490 --> 00:29:04.771
I says, "What Maller Building?"

00:29:04.771 --> 00:29:06.350
"What robbery?"

00:29:06.350 --> 00:29:09.300
He's "I know you've done
that fucking robbery."

00:29:09.300 --> 00:29:12.180
He says, "You and Dickie Gorman."

00:29:12.180 --> 00:29:14.357
I says, "You got the wrong information."

00:29:15.529 --> 00:29:16.887
He says, "I can't prove it."

00:29:18.128 --> 00:29:19.493
He says, "I just want you to know."

00:29:20.411 --> 00:29:21.667
And he says, "You can go."

00:29:24.027 --> 00:29:25.133
I didn't know at that time

00:29:25.133 --> 00:29:27.530
