00:29:27.530 --> 00:29:29.460
by the Chicago Outfit.

00:29:29.460 --> 00:29:32.010
So one of them loose mouthed guys

00:29:32.010 --> 00:29:34.510
had probably told this fucking cop.

00:29:34.510 --> 00:29:36.440
So you see what I mean?

00:29:36.440 --> 00:29:40.333
They loose mouths, loose lips, sink ships.

00:29:41.270 --> 00:29:43.020
So that's what happened.

00:29:43.989 --> 00:29:45.425
That was, that was a big one.

00:29:45.425 --> 00:29:48.029
Then I did Brinks trucks,
and all of that shit.

00:29:48.029 --> 00:29:49.230
- [Mark] What was the one
that you're famous for

00:29:49.230 --> 00:29:51.553
in down in Calumet City, Indiana?

00:29:51.553 --> 00:29:55.550
- Aw, the bank vault?

00:29:55.550 --> 00:29:57.050
- [Mark] Yeah, the bank vault.

00:29:58.049 --> 00:30:02.390
- Yeah, I'm a kid, still a
very young kid in the 50's.

00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:07.490
Tony comes to me, and he
says, "Listen, I got a score."

00:30:07.490 --> 00:30:12.107
He says, "With tree guys that
you don't know, but I know.

00:30:12.107 --> 00:30:15.617
"And Dickie and you'll be together."

00:30:17.306 --> 00:30:18.668
He says, "We're gonna do it together.

00:30:18.668 --> 00:30:21.320
"There's gonna be six
of us, a bank score."

00:30:21.320 --> 00:30:23.620
I said, "Here we go with the banks again."

00:30:23.620 --> 00:30:26.857
He says, "No, no, no, we're
gonna go into the vault."

00:30:28.374 --> 00:30:30.689
I says, "Aw, that's a new experience."

00:30:30.689 --> 00:30:31.522
I said, "All right."

00:30:32.830 --> 00:30:37.587
So I get, meet one of
the guys that was there.

00:30:37.587 --> 00:30:40.512
His name was Joe Lombardo,
and unbeknown to me

00:30:40.512 --> 00:30:43.800
that in later years, Joe
Lombardo would become our boss.

00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:45.969
He was just right then and there,

00:30:45.969 --> 00:30:48.910
Joe was working as a, he
worked the crap games,

00:30:48.910 --> 00:30:50.670
gambling in Chicago,

00:30:50.670 --> 00:30:51.900
and he's got his two friends.

00:30:51.900 --> 00:30:53.892
I don't even know who they are.

00:30:53.892 --> 00:30:54.725
I don't even know what
their fucking names are.

00:30:54.725 --> 00:30:55.558
I don't even know.

00:30:55.558 --> 00:30:56.960
I didn't care.

00:30:56.960 --> 00:30:58.940
So we all take a ride, the six of us.

00:30:58.940 --> 00:31:01.683
We go to Calumet City,

00:31:03.010 --> 00:31:06.870
and I see the bank.

00:31:06.870 --> 00:31:09.623
And then I see an empty building
next to it, right up to it.

00:31:10.533 --> 00:31:12.274
But they got two foundations.

00:31:12.274 --> 00:31:13.400
At least that's building empty.

00:31:13.400 --> 00:31:15.693
We go through the foundation,

00:31:15.693 --> 00:31:18.410
double foundation which
would make it that big.

00:31:18.410 --> 00:31:21.394
I said, "We'll be digging
a week over there,"

00:31:21.394 --> 00:31:22.227
I said, "to get through that."

00:31:22.227 --> 00:31:24.894
He said, "Well, we're getting
into the empty building.

00:31:24.894 --> 00:31:26.270
"We go down to the basement."

00:31:26.270 --> 00:31:27.373
So we figured it out.

00:31:27.373 --> 00:31:29.149
We go through the foundations.

00:31:29.149 --> 00:31:31.950
Then we know how many,
we walked off the footage

00:31:32.951 --> 00:31:35.490
from one foundation to the bank vault

00:31:35.490 --> 00:31:37.723
because the bank had a basement too.

00:31:40.489 --> 00:31:44.700
So we walked it off and come
right up underneath the vault.

00:31:44.700 --> 00:31:47.973
We get underneath the vault,
the day of the robbery.

00:31:48.885 --> 00:31:50.726
Not that day, the day of the robbery.

00:31:50.726 --> 00:31:53.576
We come equipped with two
cars, radios and all the tools.

00:31:54.664 --> 00:31:55.948
We knew we couldn't smoke.

00:31:55.948 --> 00:31:56.946
We couldn't eat.

00:31:56.946 --> 00:31:59.417
And we couldn't piss
because DNA, you know,

00:32:00.267 --> 00:32:02.246
we thought they could get that stuff then.

00:32:02.246 --> 00:32:03.643
We thought of that stuff
before they made it known.

00:32:04.640 --> 00:32:05.710
So we did all of that.

00:32:06.727 --> 00:32:08.727
And it was a lot of work, a lot of work.

00:32:09.624 --> 00:32:12.684
I mean, the hard part was
going through the floor

00:32:12.684 --> 00:32:13.688
from the basement.

00:32:13.688 --> 00:32:14.700
- [Mark] You got concrete.

00:32:14.700 --> 00:32:15.706
You got rebar.

00:32:15.706 --> 00:32:17.245
- Very, yeah, with rebar,

00:32:17.245 --> 00:32:20.664
and we had torches and tanks
and very, very difficult.

00:32:20.664 --> 00:32:22.685
And finally we get up in there,

00:32:22.685 --> 00:32:24.286
and we had a little ladder with us,

00:32:24.286 --> 00:32:26.100
and we got up in there.

00:32:26.100 --> 00:32:27.833
- [Mark] How many hours did this take?

00:32:28.758 --> 00:32:32.421
- Full day, a full day to
go through both of them.

00:32:32.421 --> 00:32:35.763
Exhausted, we were dirty and exhausted,

00:32:35.763 --> 00:32:37.030
and by the time we got in there,

00:32:37.030 --> 00:32:39.680
and we didn't have the up to date tools

00:32:40.645 --> 00:32:42.620
to open up the boxes because
there's double locks,

00:32:42.620 --> 00:32:44.726
but we managed to open them.

00:32:44.726 --> 00:32:48.480
We used the crowbars, and
hammers and chisels and sludges.

00:32:48.480 --> 00:32:50.300
We popped 'em open.

00:32:50.300 --> 00:32:53.033
We went for the bigger
boxes, the bigger boxes.

00:32:55.210 --> 00:32:59.010
Anything that was paper, useless to us.

00:32:59.010 --> 00:33:00.440
We left it there.

00:33:00.440 --> 00:33:02.403
We took the jewelry and cash.

00:33:04.159 --> 00:33:07.360
And at the end of the day, we
wound up with $750,000 cash

00:33:09.066 --> 00:33:13.066
and valued at probably a
million dollars in jewelry,

00:33:13.066 --> 00:33:14.257
but you don't get that.

00:33:14.257 --> 00:33:15.823
You get a quarter of it, you know,

00:33:15.823 --> 00:33:17.473
whatever the price is on jewelry.

00:33:18.860 --> 00:33:22.893
So then I come to find
out the Outfit gets 20%.

00:33:23.980 --> 00:33:25.080
I said, what the fuck.

00:33:26.267 --> 00:33:27.802
One of the guys didn't wanna pay.

00:33:27.802 --> 00:33:31.137
I don't know what happened
to him, but we all paid 20%.

00:33:31.137 --> 00:33:32.290
So I wind up with 50G.

00:33:32.290 --> 00:33:34.723
50G at that age, I was a millionaire.

00:33:35.624 --> 00:33:36.663
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:33:36.663 --> 00:33:38.499
- It took us a day to count the money.

00:33:38.499 --> 00:33:40.862
We brought it up to this guy's house.

00:33:40.862 --> 00:33:42.780
The one that didn't want to give 20%,

00:33:42.780 --> 00:33:47.780
and it was like a full-size bed.

00:33:50.381 --> 00:33:53.382
And I remember we got
singles, five dollar bills,

00:33:53.382 --> 00:33:56.685
twenties, hundreds, and we're putting them

00:33:56.685 --> 00:33:57.923
in thousand dollar wrappers.

00:33:59.703 --> 00:34:01.353
They covered the bed a foot high.

00:34:02.578 --> 00:34:04.433
That's how money was on
that bed, a foot high.

00:34:05.320 --> 00:34:09.858
Our hands were totally green
from counting the money,

00:34:09.858 --> 00:34:10.913
totally green, the ink.

00:34:12.340 --> 00:34:15.663
And then we took our ends out,
and we'd left outta there.

00:34:17.358 --> 00:34:19.758
The guy had his windows
blocked off, boarded up.

00:34:20.899 --> 00:34:21.790
His wife, couldn't go in the room.

00:34:21.790 --> 00:34:23.513
He put a padlock on the door,

00:34:25.717 --> 00:34:28.260
and it was a good feeling
having that kind of,

00:34:28.260 --> 00:34:30.600
I immediately went and bought a new car.

00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:32.850
I bought new cars every
time I did something.

00:34:33.916 --> 00:34:36.410
I had a reputation as a car buff.

00:34:36.410 --> 00:34:38.850
People would say when your
ashtray's full of cigarettes,

00:34:38.850 --> 00:34:40.659
you'll sell it tomorrow.

00:34:40.659 --> 00:34:41.492
I'd sell it.

00:34:41.492 --> 00:34:44.550
I'd buy cars, three,
four cars a year easy.

00:34:44.550 --> 00:34:46.854
And I like cars, you know.

