00:46:08.160 --> 00:46:10.030
He opens up the doors.

00:46:10.030 --> 00:46:12.820
I look to the right, I
look up the stairway.

00:46:12.820 --> 00:46:13.653
I'm listening.

00:46:13.653 --> 00:46:16.150
I says, "Your wife ain't home, your kids?"

00:46:16.150 --> 00:46:16.983
"Nah, nah."

00:46:16.983 --> 00:46:17.816
"You sure?"

00:46:17.816 --> 00:46:18.649
"Yeah."

00:46:18.649 --> 00:46:19.482
"Everything's cool?

00:46:19.482 --> 00:46:20.426
"Yeah."

00:46:20.426 --> 00:46:21.986
"'Cause I don't wanna talk."

00:46:21.986 --> 00:46:23.547
He turns around, boom, boom, boom.

00:46:23.547 --> 00:46:26.660
I shoot him in the back of
the, five times real quick.

00:46:26.660 --> 00:46:29.126
Bing, bing, bing, bing, bing, bing.

00:46:29.126 --> 00:46:29.959
He runs.

00:46:29.959 --> 00:46:30.792
He looks at me.

00:46:32.060 --> 00:46:34.287
Why are you doing that?

00:46:34.287 --> 00:46:37.040
I'm thinking, this guy should be dead.

00:46:37.040 --> 00:46:39.167
I was told to kill this guy

00:46:39.167 --> 00:46:41.660
with a 22 and use half loads from Tony.

00:46:41.660 --> 00:46:42.693
I did that.

00:46:44.165 --> 00:46:45.350
It was like shooting him
in the head with a cap gun,

00:46:45.350 --> 00:46:46.183
pellet gun.

00:46:48.300 --> 00:46:49.693
He runs, I chase him.

00:46:50.550 --> 00:46:55.320
When he gets into the kitchen dining area,

00:46:55.320 --> 00:46:57.883
the garage door's there,
leading into the garage.

00:46:58.770 --> 00:47:00.860
He hits the garage door button

00:47:00.860 --> 00:47:02.567
to open up their overhead door,

00:47:02.567 --> 00:47:04.950
I hear the door going up, and I hit it,

00:47:04.950 --> 00:47:06.620
and it stops the door.

00:47:06.620 --> 00:47:10.930
Stopped the door maybe
two feet, three feet.

00:47:10.930 --> 00:47:13.720
Meanwhile, he's down on
the ground between my legs.

00:47:13.720 --> 00:47:15.383
He's bleeding all over the place,

00:47:16.760 --> 00:47:19.003
and I gotta finish him.

00:47:20.145 --> 00:47:21.673
There's no way I could leave him now.

00:47:22.770 --> 00:47:24.846
There's just no way you could leave it.

00:47:24.846 --> 00:47:25.679
You're this far into it.

00:47:25.679 --> 00:47:30.679
So I ripped the cord out
of the water machine.

00:47:30.690 --> 00:47:33.226
I tie it around his neck,
and I pull it, and it breaks.

00:47:33.226 --> 00:47:36.663
This guy is not supposed to die.

00:47:37.540 --> 00:47:41.048
So now I reach over, I reach over,

00:47:41.048 --> 00:47:42.910
and I grab, they had knives

00:47:42.910 --> 00:47:44.660
in them peg boards they put them in

00:47:45.628 --> 00:47:46.627
in the kitchen.

00:47:46.627 --> 00:47:48.305
I reached over, and I grabbed it.

00:47:48.305 --> 00:47:49.605
He's still there.

00:47:49.605 --> 00:47:52.550
And just as I'm ready to come
down on him with the knife,

00:47:52.550 --> 00:47:54.253
that little garage door opens,

00:47:55.220 --> 00:47:58.340
and I'm, now I gotta, and
whoever it is, I gotta kill him.

00:47:58.340 --> 00:48:00.260
I don't wanna, but I gotta.

00:48:00.260 --> 00:48:01.650
What am I gonna do?

00:48:01.650 --> 00:48:04.593
So I go like this, it's
the guy, my partner.

00:48:05.690 --> 00:48:09.140
I go, "Jesus, you scared
the shit out of me."

00:48:09.140 --> 00:48:11.480
He said, "I counted the shots."

00:48:11.480 --> 00:48:14.846
He says, "And you didn't
come out, and I was worried."

00:48:14.846 --> 00:48:15.967
I said, "Did you hear
anything on the radio?"

00:48:15.967 --> 00:48:17.520
"No, nothing."

00:48:17.520 --> 00:48:19.520
He says, "None of the neighbors called."

00:48:20.490 --> 00:48:22.407
He said, "I brought extra bullets in."

00:48:23.902 --> 00:48:25.270
(Frank laughing) I couldn't believe it.

00:48:25.270 --> 00:48:26.826
So I take 'em.

00:48:26.826 --> 00:48:29.576
I take the shells out, put
'em in my pocket, reload it.

00:48:30.540 --> 00:48:32.030
He puts the pillow in back of his head.

00:48:32.030 --> 00:48:35.060
I put one in front, and
I emptied the bullet out

00:48:35.060 --> 00:48:38.023
in the frontal part of
his face, the bullets out.

00:48:39.340 --> 00:48:42.047
Then I say, "Come on, we'll
throw him in the pool."

00:48:42.047 --> 00:48:43.120
"Why?"

00:48:43.120 --> 00:48:45.730
He says, "Isn't that a little theatrical?"

00:48:45.730 --> 00:48:48.720
I says, "I got blood all over me."

00:48:48.720 --> 00:48:53.720
I says, "I got, from the gun,
the powder, come on, you too."

00:48:56.140 --> 00:48:58.530
Come on, drag him, throw him in the pool.

00:48:58.530 --> 00:49:01.270
We go into the pool up to our necks.

00:49:01.270 --> 00:49:03.270
The guy goes in the water, and he sinks.

00:49:04.130 --> 00:49:05.510
And we leave.

00:49:05.510 --> 00:49:06.343
That was it.

00:49:06.343 --> 00:49:08.160
Got rid of all the stuff.

00:49:08.160 --> 00:49:10.220
Came back to my place in our underwear.

00:49:10.220 --> 00:49:14.980
We rode back in our underwear,
and then I took a shower.

00:49:14.980 --> 00:49:19.080
My hands, get that shit off from the pool,

00:49:19.080 --> 00:49:22.050
and in case there was any remnants

00:49:22.050 --> 00:49:24.040
of that gunpowder, you know.

00:49:24.040 --> 00:49:25.585
So did he, later.

00:49:25.585 --> 00:49:28.033
And then I drove him to
the airport and he left.

00:49:28.905 --> 00:49:31.064
- [Mark] So when you get an order, from--

00:49:31.064 --> 00:49:32.069
- Huh?

00:49:32.069 --> 00:49:33.206
- [Mark] When you get
an order from like Tony

00:49:33.206 --> 00:49:34.240
or from somebody like
that to hit somebody.

00:49:34.240 --> 00:49:35.890
- Gotta get an okay.

00:49:35.890 --> 00:49:38.106
- [Mark] Is it something you get paid for

00:49:38.106 --> 00:49:39.060
or is just something you just do?

00:49:39.060 --> 00:49:41.160
- Whenever you're ordered to do something,

00:49:42.040 --> 00:49:46.070
when I hear people say you get
paid for it, that's bullshit.

00:49:46.070 --> 00:49:48.700
There's no paycheck for killing anybody.

00:49:48.700 --> 00:49:50.680
If they order you to kill somebody,

00:49:50.680 --> 00:49:53.130
whoever orders you that's a boss,

00:49:53.130 --> 00:49:57.080
you know that they got the
okay to tell you to do it.

00:49:57.080 --> 00:50:00.690
It goes in front of two or
three bosses, and they decide

00:50:01.790 --> 00:50:05.220
if it's right for you to kill
whoever you're gonna kill.

00:50:06.248 --> 00:50:07.868
Or they come up to you and tell you,

00:50:07.868 --> 00:50:10.810
"All right listen, you gotta
take care of so and so."

00:50:10.810 --> 00:50:11.997
You don't question it.

00:50:11.997 --> 00:50:13.190
You do it.

00:50:13.190 --> 00:50:17.667
If you don't, then you become the victim

00:50:17.667 --> 00:50:19.008
because they're not gonna come to you

00:50:19.008 --> 00:50:20.227
if they didn't think you would say,

00:50:20.227 --> 00:50:21.400
you were gonna say no.

00:50:21.400 --> 00:50:22.860
So that's the process.

00:50:22.860 --> 00:50:24.488
- [Mark] Have you ever--

00:50:24.488 --> 00:50:27.117
- So when I killed Lisner, I did ask Tony,

00:50:27.117 --> 00:50:29.329
"Did you get a okay on this?"

00:50:29.329 --> 00:50:31.279
He said, "Yes," but he didn't, he lied.

00:50:33.126 --> 00:50:34.478
I found that out later.

00:50:34.478 --> 00:50:36.240
- [Mark] Did you ever
get convicted of murder?

00:50:36.240 --> 00:50:37.073
- Convicted of it?

00:50:37.073 --> 00:50:38.260
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:50:38.260 --> 00:50:40.880
- I got immunity from prosecution.

00:50:40.880 --> 00:50:42.380
- [Mark] Which is why
you're able to talk here.

00:50:42.380 --> 00:50:45.270
- Yeah, I got immunity from prosecution

00:50:45.270 --> 00:50:47.470
as long as I cooperated
with the government.

00:50:48.326 --> 00:50:49.243
- [Mark] Yeah, we'll
get into that in a bit.

00:50:49.243 --> 00:50:50.670
- So I could freely talk
about stuff like that

00:50:50.670 --> 00:50:52.685
or else I wouldn't talk about it.

00:50:52.685 --> 00:50:54.490
And I'm not bragging
about it, first of all.

00:50:54.490 --> 00:50:56.340
You don't brag about stuff like that.

00:50:57.190 --> 00:50:58.023
It's not nice.

00:50:58.023 --> 00:51:01.680
It's not right, but it's
no different, I say,

00:51:01.680 --> 00:51:03.686
and some people say,

00:51:03.686 --> 00:51:05.630
"Well how could you put
it, compared it to?"

00:51:05.630 --> 00:51:08.266
It's no different than
being in the military

00:51:08.266 --> 00:51:11.302
and killing a lot of people
that you don't even see.

00:51:11.302 --> 00:51:12.364
- [Mark] You'd been given an order.

00:51:12.364 --> 00:51:14.042
- You know, that's it, you know.

00:51:14.042 --> 00:51:16.292
- [Mark] Yeah, do you,
I mean, so do you have

00:51:18.020 --> 00:51:20.503
like memories of these murders?

00:51:20.503 --> 00:51:21.501
- No.

00:51:21.501 --> 00:51:23.423
- [Mark] Or are their psychological
repercussions later on?

00:51:23.423 --> 00:51:25.270
Or do you stay up at night
or anything like that?

00:51:25.270 --> 00:51:30.270
- I do not have any repercussions
in thought or memory

00:51:30.520 --> 00:51:32.210
about the people I killed

00:51:32.210 --> 00:51:34.333
because I'd be in a straight jacket.

00:51:35.190 --> 00:51:38.010
It's just something you
wash out of your mind.

00:51:38.010 --> 00:51:39.293
You have to do it.

00:51:40.925 --> 00:51:42.425
And that's something I'd done.

00:51:43.943 --> 00:51:45.923
And if you can't, that's the way it is.

00:51:45.923 --> 00:51:48.245
You just, you have to get
it out out of your head.

00:51:48.245 --> 00:51:49.750
- [Mark] I think it takes
a certain personality type,

00:51:49.750 --> 00:51:52.523
certain series of traits
to be able to do that.

00:51:52.523 --> 00:51:53.830
- Well, you have to be to
start with a little strong,

00:51:53.830 --> 00:51:56.920
strong character, strong inside,

00:51:56.920 --> 00:51:59.600
a willpower to forget,

00:51:59.600 --> 00:52:01.600
you know, to try and forget I'd done it.

00:52:02.520 --> 00:52:04.320
The only time I remember this nonsense

00:52:04.320 --> 00:52:06.230
is when I'm interviewed about it.

00:52:06.230 --> 00:52:08.260
Otherwise I never talked about it.

00:52:08.260 --> 00:52:09.958
Never brag about it.

00:52:09.958 --> 00:52:10.966
- [Mark] Never comes up.

00:52:10.966 --> 00:52:11.799
- It's nothing to brag about.

00:52:11.799 --> 00:52:15.720
- [Mark] So Tony, Tony Spilotro
continues to move up, right?

00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:19.350
- Oh, yeah, by, well, he
was the boss out there.

00:52:19.350 --> 00:52:21.624
In Vegas, Tony was the boss.

00:52:21.624 --> 00:52:22.622
I was his underboss.

00:52:22.622 --> 00:52:23.730
- [Mark] Was he the boss in
Chicago when he left, or?

00:52:23.730 --> 00:52:25.842
- He was a boss in Chicago.

00:52:25.842 --> 00:52:28.570
If he went back there, he'd be a boss.

00:52:28.570 --> 00:52:30.285
You gotta remember though,

00:52:30.285 --> 00:52:33.826
if you're not in the state
that you're a boss in,

00:52:33.826 --> 00:52:35.184
and you're in another state,

00:52:35.184 --> 00:52:37.900
you don't control that state anymore.

00:52:37.900 --> 00:52:39.850
They got another guy that'll take it over.

00:52:39.850 --> 00:52:43.570
If you come back, you may
jump into that position again,

00:52:43.570 --> 00:52:46.380
whatever territory you had.

00:52:46.380 --> 00:52:51.380
It's, so he couldn't be a
boss in Chicago, excuse me.

00:52:51.677 --> 00:52:53.819
- [Mark] Yeah, so how did
your relationship with Tony

00:52:53.819 --> 00:52:54.818
change over the years?

00:52:54.818 --> 00:52:55.983
Because you started off--

00:52:55.983 --> 00:52:58.603
- Tony was getting more paranoid,
more paranoid every day.

00:52:59.461 --> 00:53:00.460
- [Mark] Right.

00:53:00.460 --> 00:53:01.921
- And I used to see it as very obvious.

00:53:01.921 --> 00:53:04.730
And, but yet he always
was in the limelight.

00:53:04.730 --> 00:53:06.930
He managed to keep
himself in the limelight.

00:53:08.300 --> 00:53:12.400
He'd always come to my
restaurant, cost me a lot of heat

00:53:12.400 --> 00:53:14.420
coming to the restaurant all the time.

00:53:14.420 --> 00:53:16.210
He caused me all this heat,

00:53:16.210 --> 00:53:18.830
trying to do a legitimate business.

00:53:18.830 --> 00:53:23.226
So he started getting more
paranoid, more paranoid.

00:53:23.226 --> 00:53:25.457
And I told him, "You
gotta slow down, Tony."

00:53:26.425 --> 00:53:27.258
"What do you mean?"

00:53:27.258 --> 00:53:29.786
I says, "I could see it's
getting a hold of you,

00:53:29.786 --> 00:53:31.020
"all this news and all of that."

00:53:31.020 --> 00:53:32.822
He says, "Well, they're lying."

00:53:32.822 --> 00:53:34.880
I said, "Of course they're
lying on a lot of things."

00:53:34.880 --> 00:53:35.977
I said, "Ignore it."

00:53:37.221 --> 00:53:39.585
He said, "You know that fucking RICO law.

00:53:39.585 --> 00:53:41.367
"They could put you in
jail for that RICO law.

00:53:41.367 --> 00:53:43.306
"They can lie all they want.

00:53:43.306 --> 00:53:44.884
"They put you in the newspaper.

00:53:44.884 --> 00:53:47.890
"They show association, put
you in jail for 20 years."

00:53:47.890 --> 00:53:50.340
Which he had a point, you know?

00:53:50.340 --> 00:53:53.900
So I start noticing it more and more.

00:53:54.900 --> 00:53:56.873
Tony was falling into,

00:53:57.870 --> 00:54:01.313
more involved with his
family, his wife and his kid.

00:54:02.190 --> 00:54:07.190
He was becoming a guy that I
felt didn't want to go to jail.

00:54:08.120 --> 00:54:10.690
Wanted to become a
family man, stay at home.

00:54:11.880 --> 00:54:13.810
He's not in Chicago now.

00:54:13.810 --> 00:54:18.810
Now his next step I thought
would be leave Vegas.

00:54:18.830 --> 00:54:20.820
Let somebody else come
out there and be the boss,

00:54:20.820 --> 00:54:22.980
or try to leave Vegas.

00:54:22.980 --> 00:54:25.900
He wanted to start a new life, I know,

00:54:25.900 --> 00:54:27.887
cause he used to say, "I'm
fed up with this shit.

00:54:27.887 --> 00:54:29.483
"I'm fed up with it."

00:54:30.343 --> 00:54:33.063
And he was happy to, you
know, have a son and a wife.

00:54:34.360 --> 00:54:36.700
So I always got strange
feelings out of that

00:54:36.700 --> 00:54:38.890
when he was doing that,

00:54:38.890 --> 00:54:42.220
and I don't know what his plans were.

00:54:42.220 --> 00:54:45.483
I'll leave that up to your
audience to figure it out.

00:54:46.500 --> 00:54:49.310
But I could see he was
getting a little tired

00:54:49.310 --> 00:54:52.813
of fighting the police, the newspapers,

00:54:54.140 --> 00:54:56.623
and he wasn't gonna run anywhere.

00:54:56.623 --> 00:54:59.530
It wasn't gonna run away,
in other words, disappear

00:54:59.530 --> 00:55:01.423
if he had a case going.

00:55:01.423 --> 00:55:03.523
He wouldn't do that because of his family.

00:55:04.600 --> 00:55:06.520
He loved them too much.

00:55:06.520 --> 00:55:07.722
He wasn't gonna leave

00:55:07.722 --> 00:55:09.480
because if you leave and go to Hong Kong

00:55:09.480 --> 00:55:12.238
or wherever you run to, they'll get you.

00:55:12.238 --> 00:55:13.173
Eventually they'll get you.

00:55:14.183 --> 00:55:15.016
The feds'll get you.

00:55:15.016 --> 00:55:17.305
Somewhere along the line they get,

00:55:17.305 --> 00:55:19.560
don't forget they got millions
and millions of dollars

00:55:19.560 --> 00:55:22.040
they get from the taxpayer, tax people,

00:55:22.040 --> 00:55:24.960
the taxpayers, I should
say, to go after you.

00:55:24.960 --> 00:55:26.690
So and he knew that.

00:55:26.690 --> 00:55:30.700
So Tony would never run,
nor would his brother.

00:55:30.700 --> 00:55:31.803
That's the way it is.

00:55:33.925 --> 00:55:35.430
- [Mark] And then
eventually something came up

00:55:35.430 --> 00:55:40.430
where he put a hit out on you, right?

00:55:41.470 --> 00:55:42.303
- He did what?

00:55:42.303 --> 00:55:44.461
- [Mark] He, there was a hit.

00:55:44.461 --> 00:55:47.013
You were in prison, but
you heard a recording?

00:55:48.130 --> 00:55:53.130
- Yeah I was pulled
into an interview room.

00:55:53.880 --> 00:55:55.473
I was found guilty on a case,

00:55:56.480 --> 00:55:58.160
and I was pulled into an interview room

00:55:58.160 --> 00:56:00.303
by a couple of agents.

00:56:01.160 --> 00:56:04.490
And they told me that there
was a contract on my life,

00:56:04.490 --> 00:56:06.503
and I told them get the fuck out of there,

00:56:06.503 --> 00:56:07.900
'cause I know the game.

00:56:07.900 --> 00:56:08.959
They play this game.

00:56:08.959 --> 00:56:09.792
They all play that game.

00:56:09.792 --> 00:56:11.810
Whether they're agents or regular locals.

00:56:11.810 --> 00:56:13.370
They have to do it.

00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:17.540
He said, "My responsibility as
a federal agent to inform you

00:56:17.540 --> 00:56:19.190
that there's a contract out on your life."

00:56:19.190 --> 00:56:21.822
I said, "Get the fuck out of here."

00:56:21.822 --> 00:56:23.380
And I told the cops,
send me down to my cell.

00:56:23.380 --> 00:56:25.502
So they bring me down., and I says,

00:56:25.502 --> 00:56:26.335
"If you're not bringing me to,"

00:56:26.335 --> 00:56:27.977
they had me in the dormitory.

00:56:27.977 --> 00:56:29.723
"You're putting me in a cell."

00:56:29.723 --> 00:56:31.900
He says, "Because there's a
contract out on your life."

00:56:31.900 --> 00:56:33.370
What the fuck?

00:56:33.370 --> 00:56:35.547
Then the radio comes on.

00:56:35.547 --> 00:56:37.400
"Bring him back upstairs."

00:56:37.400 --> 00:56:38.690
Like, again?

00:56:38.690 --> 00:56:40.890
I go back upstairs.

00:56:40.890 --> 00:56:42.720
They got this recording.

00:56:42.720 --> 00:56:45.373
They want me to hear,
listen to some message,

00:56:46.524 --> 00:56:48.110
listen to some wire taps.

00:56:48.110 --> 00:56:49.787
So I listened to the wire tap,

00:56:51.162 --> 00:56:52.660
and I hear one guy on the other end,

00:56:52.660 --> 00:56:55.603
and it's saying, "What's
going on out there in Vegas?"

00:56:55.603 --> 00:56:57.378
And Tony said, "I can't control this guy.

00:56:57.378 --> 00:56:58.211
"He's like a loose cannon."

00:56:58.211 --> 00:56:59.670
Meaning me.

00:56:59.670 --> 00:57:01.297
So the agent says, "What did you hear?"

00:57:01.297 --> 00:57:04.043
"Who do you hear listening to?"

00:57:04.043 --> 00:57:06.370
He said, I'm not ready to
talk to you about that.

00:57:06.370 --> 00:57:08.700
So he stands there silent.

00:57:08.700 --> 00:57:12.413
And then a guy says, "Well,
who's doing all them,

00:57:13.578 --> 00:57:15.130
"who's whacking people
and all them robberies?"

00:57:15.130 --> 00:57:17.317
He says, "That other guy, I'm telling you.

00:57:17.317 --> 00:57:20.178
"I can't control him," he says.

00:57:20.178 --> 00:57:23.260
"He's got a tough crew of
guys that are with him."

00:57:23.260 --> 00:57:26.021
He says, "Every day I think
they might take it over,

00:57:26.021 --> 00:57:27.263
"take me out."

00:57:27.263 --> 00:57:28.727
You know, and the guy says,

00:57:28.727 --> 00:57:30.920
"Well, then you know what you gotta do.

00:57:30.920 --> 00:57:32.964
"He's gonna make bond isn't he?"

00:57:32.964 --> 00:57:34.543
He says, "Yeah, he'll get an appeal bond."

00:57:34.543 --> 00:57:36.530
He says, "Then you gotta
clean your dirty laundry."

00:57:36.530 --> 00:57:37.940
Well, fuck.

00:57:37.940 --> 00:57:39.990
Let me tell you something.

00:57:39.990 --> 00:57:43.800
I've had 39 friends in
my lifetime, maybe more,

00:57:43.800 --> 00:57:46.730
that were killed by the Outfit.

00:57:46.730 --> 00:57:48.913
I didn't wanna be 39 or 40.

00:57:50.270 --> 00:57:52.550
So I went back down to the cell.

00:57:52.550 --> 00:57:55.020
I thought about it overnight,

00:57:55.020 --> 00:57:56.637
got up in the morning, and I told him,

00:57:56.637 --> 00:57:59.138
"Get a hold of that agent that was there.

00:57:59.138 --> 00:58:01.417
"I wanna, just get a hold of that agent,

00:58:01.417 --> 00:58:02.627
"I wanna talk to him."

00:58:03.643 --> 00:58:06.070
- [Mark] But this is, this
is, the recording was Tony.

00:58:06.070 --> 00:58:08.281
- Yeah, it was Tony.

00:58:08.281 --> 00:58:09.378
- [Mark] And this is somebody
that you've been tight with

00:58:09.378 --> 00:58:10.760
for how long?

00:58:10.760 --> 00:58:12.943
- We were 12 years old.

00:58:12.943 --> 00:58:15.119
I don't know how many
years, I was 48 or 49

00:58:15.119 --> 00:58:16.240
when I rolled I think.

00:58:16.240 --> 00:58:17.073
- [Mark] But you were very close.

00:58:17.073 --> 00:58:21.420
- Oh, when these guys,
when I heard them said it,

00:58:21.420 --> 00:58:23.047
my eyes started watering, you know,

00:58:23.047 --> 00:58:24.903
'cause it broke my heart.

00:58:26.143 --> 00:58:29.060
I don't give a shit about jail.

00:58:29.060 --> 00:58:32.390
Jail, it's just an inconvenience.

00:58:32.390 --> 00:58:34.910
Guys like us make it in there.

00:58:34.910 --> 00:58:37.521
It's not some place you look to go to

00:58:37.521 --> 00:58:39.450
or relish the thought,
oh, I can't wait to go.

00:58:39.450 --> 00:58:42.264
If you could avoid it, of
course, you're gonna avoid it.

00:58:42.264 --> 00:58:46.983
But to hear this guy talk
about wanting to kill me,

00:58:46.983 --> 00:58:47.870
having to kill me,

00:58:47.870 --> 00:58:51.440
and taking all the weight off
himself and pushing it on me,

00:58:51.440 --> 00:58:53.673
it bothered me, troubling me deeply.

00:58:55.120 --> 00:59:00.120
But it took a lot for
me to become a witness.

00:59:00.650 --> 00:59:02.133
I wasn't raised this way.

00:59:03.550 --> 00:59:08.060
It took me 25 years to get over the fact

00:59:08.060 --> 00:59:09.950
that I was a witness.

00:59:09.950 --> 00:59:12.750
25 years I hated myself.

00:59:12.750 --> 00:59:15.043
25, and I'm bullshitting nobody.

00:59:17.380 --> 00:59:20.660
But then I became, actually,
I'm a religious guy now.

00:59:20.660 --> 00:59:21.623
I really am,

00:59:22.550 --> 00:59:26.093
and all these things are behind me,

00:59:27.210 --> 00:59:28.603
and I done the right thing.

00:59:29.560 --> 00:59:31.593
He was dishonorable to me.

00:59:33.120 --> 00:59:36.540
I would have probably got killed
in jail or on the streets.

00:59:36.540 --> 00:59:37.373
- [Mark] Right, either way.

00:59:37.373 --> 00:59:39.379
- I made the wise choice.

00:59:39.379 --> 00:59:42.200
It was difficult for me
to also become a witness

00:59:42.200 --> 00:59:45.713
because of my mother and my
family, my sister and brother.

00:59:46.760 --> 00:59:49.190
You know, I don't want
'em to be disgraced.

00:59:49.190 --> 00:59:51.941
They'd have to live with that
'cause they're still living

00:59:51.941 --> 00:59:54.520
in that area or were living in that area.

00:59:54.520 --> 00:59:56.950
But time goes by and time heals all.

00:59:56.950 --> 00:59:57.960
It does.

00:59:57.960 --> 01:00:00.850
25 years later, I could
go back to that city.

01:00:00.850 --> 01:00:02.950
I could, I was back there recently.

01:00:02.950 --> 01:00:04.070
I could go anywhere I want.

01:00:04.070 --> 01:00:05.260
Nobody bothers me.

01:00:05.260 --> 01:00:07.140
They all understand.

01:00:07.140 --> 01:00:10.010
They understand why I rolled.

01:00:10.010 --> 01:00:11.330
They didn't like it at first.

01:00:11.330 --> 01:00:12.633
They were very mad.

01:00:13.720 --> 01:00:17.460
They said, why would
he do that, meaning me.

01:00:17.460 --> 01:00:20.260
Somebody had a fuck him around pretty good

01:00:21.442 --> 01:00:23.200
for him to do that 'cause
he's a standup guy.

01:00:23.200 --> 01:00:24.453
They're referring to me.

01:00:26.600 --> 01:00:30.290
What the fuck did, they referred
to Tony as the little guy?

01:00:30.290 --> 01:00:32.500
What did that little guy do to him?

01:00:32.500 --> 01:00:35.880
They were starting to dislike Tony a lot

01:00:35.880 --> 01:00:38.941
because of his brother, the two of 'em.

01:00:38.941 --> 01:00:40.393
And that's it.

01:00:41.759 --> 01:00:43.663
- [Mark] Well, that's the
ultimate fuck around isn't it?

01:00:43.663 --> 01:00:44.662
- I can't hear ya.

01:00:44.662 --> 01:00:45.939
- [Mark] That's the ultimate
fuck around, isn't it?

01:00:45.939 --> 01:00:47.990
Somebody fucking, they're
trying to kill you.

01:00:47.990 --> 01:00:49.340
- Yeah, you know, I mean, come on.

01:00:49.340 --> 01:00:54.340
You know, I mean, like I
said, 39, 40 guys I know

01:00:55.819 --> 01:01:00.819
who were whacked, thinking,
well, I'm gonna be all right.

01:01:01.583 --> 01:01:02.416
They ain't gonna do it to me.

01:01:02.416 --> 01:01:04.370
They like me too much.

01:01:04.370 --> 01:01:06.923
Your best friend brings
you to the gallows, boom.

01:01:08.340 --> 01:01:09.740
That's it.

01:01:09.740 --> 01:01:11.240
- [Mark] Yeah.

01:01:11.240 --> 01:01:12.073
- Okay?

01:01:12.941 --> 01:01:15.320
- [Mark] So Tony, what
happened to him eventually?

01:01:15.320 --> 01:01:18.000
What happened to Tony eventually, he?

01:01:18.000 --> 01:01:20.717
- Tony was, eventually,
you live by the sword,

01:01:20.717 --> 01:01:22.043
you die by the sword.

01:01:23.340 --> 01:01:24.903
Eventually Tony was murdered.

01:01:26.190 --> 01:01:29.679
And I told, well, I got a call.

01:01:29.679 --> 01:01:31.760
I was in the witness protection program,

01:01:31.760 --> 01:01:34.640
an FBI guy, his name was Dennis Armley.

01:01:34.640 --> 01:01:39.487
He said to me, "Tony and his
brother Michael disappeared."

01:01:40.459 --> 01:01:42.557
He said, "Where did they run to?"

01:01:43.979 --> 01:01:45.340
I said, "They didn't run anywhere."

01:01:45.340 --> 01:01:47.430
He says, "How do you know that?"

01:01:47.430 --> 01:01:50.960
I say, "I know Tony, they're dead."

01:01:50.960 --> 01:01:53.017
He said, "How do you?"

01:01:53.017 --> 01:01:54.444
I said, "I don't know, I'm
telling you they're dead.

01:01:54.444 --> 01:01:55.277
"Tony's not gonna run."

01:01:55.277 --> 01:01:56.110
I'm on the telephone.

01:01:57.120 --> 01:01:57.953
I'm in Mobile, Alabama.

01:01:57.953 --> 01:02:00.440
This agent's calling me from Vegas.

01:02:00.440 --> 01:02:01.678
- [Mark] That where
your witness protection?

01:02:01.678 --> 01:02:03.520
- Well that was one of
the first spots I went.

01:02:03.520 --> 01:02:04.420
- [Mark] Yeah.

01:02:04.420 --> 01:02:05.283
- And he says,

01:02:06.617 --> 01:02:09.630
"Well, I'll get back to
you in a couple days."

01:02:09.630 --> 01:02:11.550
Couple days later, he didn't
have to get back to me.

01:02:11.550 --> 01:02:13.321
It was on the news

01:02:13.321 --> 01:02:17.150
that they'd discovered
the bodies in a cornfield.

01:02:17.150 --> 01:02:20.890
And he said, "Where do you
suppose they were killed?"

01:02:20.890 --> 01:02:23.433
They have dust in their lungs.

01:02:24.624 --> 01:02:27.242
They weren't killed in no cornfield.

01:02:27.242 --> 01:02:29.870
I said, 'cause they got
dust in their lungs,

01:02:29.870 --> 01:02:31.303
probably when they threw 'em in there,

01:02:32.362 --> 01:02:33.195
that dirt flew up in their mouth.

01:02:34.103 --> 01:02:38.137
I said, "They were killed in
either Cicero or Bensenville."

01:02:39.635 --> 01:02:41.655
Eventually you'll find out.

01:02:41.655 --> 01:02:42.630
And I was right.

01:02:42.630 --> 01:02:44.980
There were killed in
Bensenville in a basement.

01:02:45.840 --> 01:02:48.427
He said, "Well, they
were beaten to death."

01:02:49.710 --> 01:02:52.520
That tells you right then and there.

01:02:52.520 --> 01:02:54.980
It was in a residential area.

01:02:54.980 --> 01:02:57.191
I'm telling this agent this.

01:02:57.191 --> 01:02:58.250
It was residential.

01:02:58.250 --> 01:02:59.793
They can't use a gun.

01:03:00.639 --> 01:03:01.645
They could use knives.

01:03:01.645 --> 01:03:02.652
They could choke him.

01:03:02.652 --> 01:03:03.652
They could kick him.

01:03:03.652 --> 01:03:04.906
They could beat him.

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:06.637
He said, "Well, there was
no physical marks or bruises

01:03:06.637 --> 01:03:08.670
"all over their faces and back."

01:03:08.670 --> 01:03:11.340
Then they beat 'em with the metal bats

01:03:11.340 --> 01:03:14.193
or they kicked 'em or they
punched 'em, whatever.

01:03:14.193 --> 01:03:15.533
But they beat 'em to death.

01:03:15.533 --> 01:03:16.713
- [Mark] So when the hit is--

01:03:16.713 --> 01:03:18.675
- I didn't like the idea of that,

01:03:18.675 --> 01:03:19.570
but I didn't like, you
know, it bothered me.

01:03:19.570 --> 01:03:20.860
It really bothered me

01:03:20.860 --> 01:03:23.200
that they were killed like
that, in that fashion.

01:03:23.200 --> 01:03:25.080
But I did understand why

01:03:25.080 --> 01:03:27.951
because they couldn't make, shoot 'em.

01:03:27.951 --> 01:03:28.990
- [Mark] So when a hit
is put out on somebody,

01:03:28.990 --> 01:03:32.270
is it typically guns,
knives, baseball bats?

01:03:32.270 --> 01:03:34.270
- Whatever you choose to do.

01:03:34.270 --> 01:03:35.950
Whatever it calls for in that area

01:03:35.950 --> 01:03:37.706
- [Mark] Whatever works.

01:03:37.706 --> 01:03:40.590
- Yeah, if you choose
the, you could use a 45,

01:03:40.590 --> 01:03:42.690
use a 45, use a 22, use a 22.

01:03:42.690 --> 01:03:43.760
You've gotta use the knife,

01:03:43.760 --> 01:03:44.870
you've gotta use the knife.

01:03:44.870 --> 01:03:47.670
Whatever the situation calls for.

01:03:47.670 --> 01:03:49.800
You gotta use dynamite, use dynamite.

01:03:49.800 --> 01:03:51.413
Riga caro, whatever it is.

01:03:52.251 --> 01:03:55.170
- [Mark] So what do you think the, I mean,

01:03:55.170 --> 01:03:57.330
I'm trying to get a handle
on the psychological traits

01:03:57.330 --> 01:03:59.568
of somebody that has a life of crime

01:03:59.568 --> 01:04:02.985
as opposed to like say just a
regular law-abiding citizen.

01:04:02.985 --> 01:04:03.818
- A regular Mickey the Mope.

01:04:04.755 --> 01:04:08.130
Yeah, you know, I respect people that,

01:04:08.130 --> 01:04:10.720
and I'm not bullshitting
any of you's right now.

01:04:10.720 --> 01:04:14.153
I respect a man that
works from nine to five.

01:04:15.230 --> 01:04:17.330
They make good money, and they save money.

01:04:19.233 --> 01:04:21.700
This is the life they choose to live,

01:04:21.700 --> 01:04:24.790
and God bless them for it.

01:04:24.790 --> 01:04:28.470
I choose the life I wanted to live

01:04:28.470 --> 01:04:30.923
is because I found it glamorous.

01:04:32.150 --> 01:04:35.220
I did find out that money don't last long

01:04:35.220 --> 01:04:38.330
'cause easy, and it's
not easy come either,

01:04:38.330 --> 01:04:39.850
but I'm gonna use that term.

01:04:39.850 --> 01:04:41.830
Easy come, easy go.

01:04:41.830 --> 01:04:45.340
You gotta remember,
we're up 24 hours a day,

01:04:45.340 --> 01:04:46.940
thinking and robbing.

01:04:46.940 --> 01:04:49.970
Business guy or a guy
that works for a living,

01:04:49.970 --> 01:04:52.170
he's sleeping eight, nine hours.

01:04:52.170 --> 01:04:53.720
We're out there spending money.

01:04:54.570 --> 01:04:58.920
So you, most guys that were
in the Outfit died broke,

01:04:58.920 --> 01:05:00.590
died busted.

01:05:00.590 --> 01:05:03.252
I'm not even gonna go into that list.

01:05:03.252 --> 01:05:05.310
There's only a few that had
a lot of money at the end,

01:05:05.310 --> 01:05:07.269
only a few.

01:05:07.269 --> 01:05:09.280
You spend money, you got too many hours.

01:05:09.280 --> 01:05:12.920
I respect the working-class people a lot.

01:05:12.920 --> 01:05:17.043
Now some of these white
collar crimes, another story.

01:05:19.420 --> 01:05:21.500
Biggest crooks in the world.

01:05:21.500 --> 01:05:23.760
Let's go to Washington D.C.

01:05:23.760 --> 01:05:25.409
- [Mark] Yeah.

01:05:25.409 --> 01:05:26.242
